2. //!
3. //! The bit→description table is NOT on the `platform-bridge`, so it is replicated
4. //! here as a Rust const (analysis §3.4) — error decode must be byte-identical to the
5. //! e2e assertions (`test_status_error.py`). The masks + decode helpers
6. //! (`is_error_block_eeprom_reading`, `fetch_generic_error_description`,
7. //! `detect_port_in_error_status`) drive the `SfpStateUpdateTask` error branch (M1) and
8. //! the DOM error-status gate (M4).
9. #![allow(dead_code, unused_variables, unused_imports)]
